# Redstone torch burnout drive. Rows are TICK DX DY DZ BLOCK META, offsets
# relative to the torch position; the driven cell is the torch's support block.
#
# Format and scene adopted from bluecoconut's PR #5
# (magma/trace/fixtures/redstone_torch_floor_burnout.sequence). Coordinates are
# re-anchored to DX=0 DY=-1 DZ=0 - the block directly under a floor-standing
# torch, meta 5 - because this gate builds its scene through setblocks_locked
# rather than their oracle fixture loader.
#
# Mechanism (java/oracle-src/net/minecraft/block/BlockRedstoneTorch.java):
# powering the support makes shouldBeOff() true, so the scheduled updateTick
# swaps lit->unlit and appends a Toggle(pos, totalWorldTime) to the static
# per-World toggle list. tickRate is 2, so a 2-tick square wave drives one
# toggle per cycle. isBurnedOut() counts entries matching the position and
# returns true at 8; updateTick prunes entries older than 60 ticks from the
# head, so all eight must land inside that window. Block 152 is the redstone
# block (a constant power source), block 1 is plain stone (unpowered).
#
# Eight lit->unlit transitions inside 32 ticks, which is comfortably inside the
# 60-tick prune window with room for the capsule boundary to land mid-run.
0 0 -1 0 152 0
2 0 -1 0 1 0
4 0 -1 0 152 0
6 0 -1 0 1 0
8 0 -1 0 152 0
10 0 -1 0 1 0
12 0 -1 0 152 0
14 0 -1 0 1 0
16 0 -1 0 152 0
18 0 -1 0 1 0
20 0 -1 0 152 0
22 0 -1 0 1 0
24 0 -1 0 152 0
26 0 -1 0 1 0
28 0 -1 0 152 0
30 0 -1 0 1 0
